// EXPLORATORY DRAFT — BLOCKED on TASK-0301.
//
// TASK-0297 cycle 117 attempted to ship this as an M5 capstone cell
// for example 07-matmul. Empirically confirmed (via inspection of
// pthreads-sync emit) that the schedule lowers without errors, but
// the host-side gather of `b` is silently mis-sliced: transfer_inject
// constructs xfer tiles with `bounds = [(i, i_band_for_w)]` for EVERY
// data symbol, then `backend_common::multi_worker_walker::wait_slice`
// treats `tile.bounds[0]` as a slice of `data.dim[0]`. b is indexed
// by [k][j] — its leading dim is k, NOT i. So `i_band` silently
// slices the k axis of b, and worker 0 receives `b[k=0..4][full j]`
// instead of `b[full k][full j]`. The compute loop reads b[k][j] for
// k=0..N regardless, so for k=i_band.end..N it reads the zero-default
// of its b buffer — wrong result.
//
// Root cause: `nucleus/backend-common/src/multi_worker_walker.rs`
// lines 919-935 documents the AXIS-MAPPING ASSUMPTION:
// "tile.bounds[i].iter_var maps to data dim i". This holds for stencil-
// shape algorithms where every data symbol is indexed by the partitioned
// iv (05-stencil, 06-separable-filter). Matmul is the first algorithm
// where it breaks (b is not indexed by i; a is not indexed by j).
//
// Fix shape: transfer_inject should construct per-data tile bounds,
// filtering `partition_axis_order` to include only axes that index
// the specific data symbol. The per-firing index expressions are
// already carried on `DataflowEdge::data_in_access` /
// `data_out_access` (see transfer_inject.rs docs §"Per-tile hoist
// for `block=N`"); the filter is one upstream pass away.
//
// Filed as TASK-0301 (HIGH). This draft schedule stays here as the
// validation target when TASK-0301 lands — at that point, add the
// corresponding e2e cells in nuc-nucleus/e2e-matrix.toml and promote
// to [[required]] M5.
//
// DO NOT add this schedule to e2e-matrix.toml today — it would
// silently fail bit-identical on every backend (mis-sliced b).

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_a on host;
    place load_b on host;
    place save_c on host;
    place madd   on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Row-band partition the outer i axis. N=16, 4 workers → 4 rows each.
    // Each worker computes c[i_band][full j] using a[i_band][full k] and
    // b[full k][full j]. Today b is silently mis-sliced — see TASK-0301.
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // All sync transfers (sync-only schedule lowers on every tier-1
    // backend once TASK-0301 lands).
    transfer a : sync;
    transfer b : sync;
    transfer c : sync;
}
